Theorem RL-6: Unique admits same-identity mutation when local safety holds

  Preconditions:
    - Uniqueness(v) = Unique and Access(v) = Owned.
    - DP-5 proves whether local borrows permit same-identity mutation.
    - DP-9's historical `StaticUnique` / `StaticShared` labels denote neutral
      SameIdentityAdmissible / IsolationRequired outcomes.

  Soundness property:
    Forall owned Unique value v at a mutation point:
      (P1) DP-5 true -> SameIdentityAdmissible.
      (P2) DP-5 false -> IsolationRequired.
      (P3) either outcome preserves evaluator value semantics when satisfied.
    No premise names a sharing check, branch, copy, counter, or storage layout.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate three cases:
      unique_no_borrow_static_inplace -> SameIdentityAdmissible
      unique_disjoint_borrow_static_inplace -> SameIdentityAdmissible
      unique_overlapping_borrow_static_shared -> IsolationRequired
    Coverage gate: 3 cases.

    Negative-direction witness:
      SameIdentityAdmissible with an overlapping live borrow is rejected because
      the borrowed view would observe another value's mutation.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl6_static_unique_mutation)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-6 enumerates Unique mutation outcomes and freezes same-identity admissibility or isolation without selecting a physical COW mechanism
